From 58c9bfaf84ee3ecc938929b7cf0ae07967e31f4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amin Roudaki <roudaky@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 12:16:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [Core] Opt-in per-request return of the last hidden states in
 generation (MRV2)

Add `SamplingParams.return_last_hidden_states`. When set, each generated
token's CompletionOutput row carries the hidden state its logits were computed
from (the input to the model's `compute_logits`; for most decoder models the
last layer's output after the final norm), in
`CompletionOutput.last_hidden_states`, shaped [num_generated_tokens,
hidden_size] in the model dtype, returned with the final output.

The engine must be started with `enable_return_last_hidden_states=True`
(`--enable-return-last-hidden-states`); otherwise such requests are rejected
at validation. With the flag off the runner holds no state and does no work;
with it on, only requests that ask pay: one gather of their logits rows per
step and a device-to-host copy on the output copy stream, carried through
ModelRunnerOutput, EngineCoreOutput (field appended last) and the output
processor like the existing per-request outputs.

Model Runner V2 only; rejected with speculative decoding, pipeline parallelism
and context parallelism (not yet validated).

Tests: scheduler routing and truncation to kept tokens; output-processor
accumulation, aggregation, and returned rows that never alias a received
transport frame; request validation; config guards; and a GPU end-to-end
test (rows per token, rows reproduce the engine's raw logits, asking changes
no other output: equal token ids, logits and rows within four fp16 ULPs).
Docs: docs/features/last_hidden_states.md. Example:
examples/generate/last_hidden_states_offline.py.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (Anthropic)
Signed-off-by: Amin Roudaki <roudaky@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 4b786f9bd2204354dcb6c0d1ad0fb4d6cd0944e0)
